[2026-03-16T01:35:24.072Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017yJjjpoNvMupWEVvsAzoRi","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# AirbnbClone Test Specification\n     2→\n     3→## Page: Login / Register (`/login`)\n     4→\n     5→<!-- Components: LoginForm, RegisterForm, AuthToggle -->\n     6→\n     7→### Component: AuthToggle\n     8→\n     9→#### Test: Auth page defaults to login mode\n    10→- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/login` for the first time (not logged in).\n    11→- **Expected:** The page displays in login mode with the email input field visible, a \"Log In\" submit button, and a toggle link reading \"Don't have an account? Register\" at the bottom.\n    12→\n    13→#### Test: Toggle from login to register mode\n    14→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode.\n    15→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Don't have an account? Register\" link.\n    16→- **Expected:** The form switches to register mode showing name and email fields, a \"Register\" submit button, and the toggle link changes to \"Already have an account? Log In\".\n    17→\n    18→#### Test: Toggle from register back to login mode\n    19→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode.\n    20→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Already have an account? Log In\" link.\n    21→- **Expected:** The form switches back to login mode with only the email field and \"Log In\" button visible.\n    22→\n    23→#### Test: Toggle preserves no stale input between modes\n    24→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode.\n    25→- **Action:** User types \"test@example.com\" in the email field, then toggles to register mode.\n    26→- **Expected:** The register form fields are empty (no carried-over email value).\n    27→\n    28→### Component: LoginForm\n    29→\n    30→#### Test: Login with valid email redirects to home\n    31→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode. A user with email \"guest@example.com\" exists in the database.\n    32→- **Action:** User types \"guest@example.com\" in the email input and clicks the \"Log In\" button.\n    33→- **Expected:** The app calls `POST /api/auth` with the email, stores the returned user object in Redux state, and redirects to the home page (`/`).\n    34→\n    35→#### Test: Login with empty email shows validation error\n    36→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode.\n    37→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Log In\" button without entering an email.\n    38→- **Expected:** A validation error message is displayed (e.g., \"Email is required\"). No API call is made.\n    39→\n    40→#### Test: Login with invalid email format shows validation error\n    41→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode.\n    42→- **Action:** User types \"not-an-email\" in the email field and clicks \"Log In\".\n    43→- **Expected:** A validation error message is displayed (e.g., \"Please enter a valid email address\"). No API call is made.\n    44→\n    45→#### Test: Login with non-existent email shows error\n    46→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode. No user with email \"unknown@example.com\" exists.\n    47→- **Action:** User types \"unknown@example.com\" and clicks \"Log In\".\n    48→- **Expected:** An error message is displayed (e.g., \"No account found with this email\"). The user remains on the login page.\n    49→\n    50→#### Test: Login form email input is functional on repeated use\n    51→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode.\n    52→- **Action:** User types \"wrong@example.com\", submits and gets an error, then clears the field, types \"guest@example.com\", and clicks \"Log In\" again.\n    53→- **Expected:** The second submission succeeds, the user is logged in and redirected to home.\n    54→\n    55→### Component: RegisterForm\n    56→\n    57→#### Test: Register with valid name and email creates account and redirects to home\n    58→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode. No user with email \"newuser@example.com\" exists.\n    59→- **Action:** User types \"New User\" in the name field and \"newuser@example.com\" in the email field, then clicks \"Register\".\n    60→- **Expected:** The app calls `POST /api/auth` with name and email, stores the returned user object in Redux state, and redirects to the home page (`/`).\n    61→\n    62→#### Test: Register with empty name shows validation error\n    63→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode.\n    64→- **Action:** User types \"newuser@example.com\" in the email field but leaves the name field empty, then clicks \"Register\".\n    65→- **Expected:** A validation error is displayed (e.g., \"Name is required\"). No API call is made.\n    66→\n    67→#### Test: Register with empty email shows validation error\n    68→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode.\n    69→- **Action:** User types \"New User\" in the name field but leaves the email field empty, then clicks \"Register\".\n    70→- **Expected:** A validation error is displayed (e.g., \"Email is required\"). No API call is made.\n    71→\n    72→#### Test: Register with invalid email format shows validation error\n    73→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode.\n    74→- **Action:** User types \"New User\" in the name field and \"bad-email\" in the email field, then clicks \"Register\".\n    75→- **Expected:** A validation error is displayed (e.g., \"Please enter a valid email address\"). No API call is made.\n    76→\n    77→#### Test: Register with already-existing email shows error\n    78→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode. A user with email \"existing@example.com\" already exists.\n    79→- **Action:** User types \"Some Name\" in the name field and \"existing@example.com\" in the email field, then clicks \"Register\".\n    80→- **Expected:** An error message is displayed (e.g., \"An account with this email already exists\"). The user remains on the register form.\n    81→\n    82→#### Test: Register form fields are functional on repeated use\n    83→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode.\n    84→- **Action:** User fills in name and an already-existing email, submits and gets an error, then changes the email to a new unique email and clicks \"Register\" again.\n    85→- **Expected:** The second submission succeeds, the user is registered and redirected to home.\n    86→\n    87→### Component: E2E Auth Flow\n    88→\n    89→#### Test: Complete signup, signout, and signin flow\n    90→- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/login` (not logged in). No account exists for the test email.\n    91→- **Action:** User toggles to register mode, fills in a unique name and email, and clicks \"Register\". After being redirected to the home page, the user opens the sidebar menu and clicks \"Log out\". The user then navigates to `/login`, enters the same email used during registration, and clicks \"Log In\".\n    92→- **Expected:** After registration, the user is redirected to the home page (`/`). After logging out, a \"Log in\" link is visible in the header. After logging in with the previously registered email, the user is redirected back to the home page (`/`), confirming the account was persisted and the full auth round-trip works.\n    93→\n    94→## Page: Home / Search (`/`)\n    95→\n    96→<!-- Components: SearchBar, CategoryFilter, PropertyGrid, PropertyCard, FavoriteButton, FiltersPanel, Pagination -->\n    97→\n    98→### Component: SearchBar\n    99→\n   100→#### Test: Search bar displays all input fields on load\n   101→- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page (`/`).\n   102→- **Expected:** The search bar is visible at the top of the page containing four inputs: a location text input with placeholder \"Where are you going?\", a check-in date picker, a check-out date picker, and a guest count selector. A search/submit button with a magnifying glass icon is visible.\n   103→\n   104→#### Test: Search by location filters property results\n   105→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties exist in \"Paris\", \"New York\", and \"Tokyo\".\n   106→- **Action:** User types \"Paris\" into the location input and clicks the search button.\n   107→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties where the city matches \"Paris\". Properties in other cities are not displayed.\n   108→\n   109→#### Test: Search by check-in and check-out dates filters results\n   110→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Some properties have bookings that overlap with the selected dates.\n   111→- **Action:** User selects a check-in date of \"2026-04-01\" and a check-out date of \"2026-04-05\" using the date pickers, then clicks the search button.\n   112→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties that are available (not fully booked) for the selected date range. The date pickers display the selected dates in a readable format.\n   113→\n   114→#### Test: Search by guest count filters results\n   115→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties exist with max_guests values of 2, 4, and 8.\n   116→- **Action:** User sets the guest count to 5 and clicks the search button.\n   117→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties where max_guests >= 5. Properties with fewer guest capacity are hidden.\n   118→\n   119→#### Test: Combined search with all fields filters results\n   120→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Multiple properties exist with varying locations, availability, and guest capacities.\n   121→- **Action:** User types \"New York\" in the location field, selects check-in \"2026-05-10\" and check-out \"2026-05-15\", sets guests to 3, and clicks the search button.\n   122→- **Expected:** The property grid shows only properties in New York that are available for those dates and accommodate at least 3 guests.\n   123→\n   124→#### Test: Clearing search fields and re-searching shows all results\n   125→- **Initial state:** User has performed a search for \"Paris\" and the grid shows filtered results.\n   126→- **Action:** User clears the location field (making it empty) and clicks the search button.\n   127→- **Expected:** The property grid resets to show all properties (unfiltered by location).\n   128→\n   129→#### Test: Search bar is functional on repeated use\n   130→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   131→- **Action:** User searches for \"Paris\", views results, then clears the location field, types \"Tokyo\", and searches again.\n   132→- **Expected:** The first search shows only Paris properties. After the second search, the grid updates to show only Tokyo properties. The location input correctly reflects \"Tokyo\".\n   133→\n   134→#### Test: Check-in date picker prevents selecting past dates\n   135→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   136→- **Action:** User opens the check-in date picker.\n   137→- **Expected:** Dates before today are disabled/grayed out and cannot be selected.\n   138→\n   139→#### Test: Check-out date must be after check-in date\n   140→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page and has selected a check-in date of \"2026-04-10\".\n   141→- **Action:** User opens the check-out date picker.\n   142→- **Expected:** Dates on or before \"2026-04-10\" are disabled/grayed out and cannot be selected. Only dates after the check-in date are selectable.\n   143→\n   144→#### Test: Guest count selector enforces minimum of 1\n   145→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   146→- **Action:** User interacts with the guest count selector.\n   147→- **Expected:** The minimum selectable value is 1. The user cannot set the guest count to 0 or a negative number.\n   148→\n   149→### Component: CategoryFilter\n   150→\n   151→#### Test: Category filter bar displays all property type chips\n   152→- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page (`/`).\n   153→- **Expected:** A horizontal scrollable bar of category chips is displayed below the search bar. Chips are shown for each property type: \"Apartment\", \"House\", \"Cabin\", \"Villa\", \"Condo\", \"Loft\", \"Cottage\", \"Townhouse\". No chip is selected by default (all properties are shown).\n   154→\n   155→#### Test: Clicking a category chip filters properties by that type\n   156→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties of various types exist (apartments, houses, cabins, etc.).\n   157→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cabin\" chip.\n   158→- **Expected:** The \"Cabin\" chip becomes visually selected/highlighted (e.g., bold outline or filled background). The property grid updates to show only properties with property_type \"Cabin\".\n   159→\n   160→#### Test: Clicking the selected category chip deselects it and shows all properties\n   161→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the \"Cabin\" chip currently selected.\n   162→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cabin\" chip again.\n   163→- **Expected:** The \"Cabin\" chip returns to its unselected appearance. The property grid shows all properties again (no category filter applied).\n   164→\n   165→#### Test: Switching between category chips updates the filter\n   166→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the \"Cabin\" chip selected, showing only cabin properties.\n   167→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Villa\" chip.\n   168→- **Expected:** The \"Cabin\" chip becomes unselected and the \"Villa\" chip becomes selected/highlighted. The property grid updates to show only properties with property_type \"Villa\".\n   169→\n   170→#### Test: Category filter works in combination with search bar\n   171→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties exist: a cabin in Paris, an apartment in Paris, and a cabin in Tokyo.\n   172→- **Action:** User types \"Paris\" in the search bar location field and clicks search, then clicks the \"Cabin\" chip.\n   173→- **Expected:** The property grid shows only cabin properties in Paris. Both the search and category filters are applied simultaneously.\n   174→\n   175→#### Test: Category filter bar is horizontally scrollable when chips overflow\n   176→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page on a narrow viewport where all chips don't fit in one row.\n   177→- **Expected:** The category filter bar is horizontally scrollable. The user can scroll left/right to see all property type chips.\n   178→\n   179→#### Test: Category chip is functional on repeated use\n   180→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   181→- **Action:** User clicks \"Apartment\" (filtered), then clicks \"House\" (switches filter), then clicks \"House\" again (deselects), then clicks \"Cabin\" (filtered again).\n   182→- **Expected:** Each click correctly updates the selected chip and the property grid filters. The final state shows only cabin properties with the \"Cabin\" chip highlighted.\n   183→\n   184→### Component: PropertyGrid\n   185→\n   186→#### Test: Property grid displays properties in a responsive grid layout\n   187→- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page. Multiple properties exist in the database.\n   188→- **Expected:** Properties are displayed in a responsive grid: 1 column on mobile, 2 columns on tablet, 3-4 columns on desktop. Each property is rendered as a PropertyCard.\n   189→\n   190→#### Test: Property grid shows message when no properties match filters\n   191→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   192→- **Action:** User searches for a location with no matching properties (e.g., \"Atlantis\").\n   193→- **Expected:** The property grid area displays a \"No properties found\" message instead of an empty grid. The message suggests adjusting filters or search criteria.\n   194→\n   195→#### Test: Property grid loads and displays properties from API on initial page load\n   196→- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page. Properties exist in the database.\n   197→- **Expected:** The grid fetches properties via `GET /api/properties` and displays property cards. While loading, a loading indicator is shown. Once loaded, the property cards appear with correct data.\n   198→\n   199→### Component: PropertyCard\n   200→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015mHckA24UDTvDqWytokBhE","session_id":"d8954074-381a-4a26-bc92-1002d48c1ee8","uuid":"653b892c-31f4-46a0-9849-7011d88e4070"}
