[2026-03-16T01:35:28.392Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01DvfKQcCqmgqgBboqUaJWCg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UVzksPLh8Q5sWkAVjZ1jti","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/docs/tests.md","offset":500,"limit":400},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6814,"cache_read_input_tokens":39935,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6814,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015mHckA24UDTvDqWytokBhE","session_id":"d8954074-381a-4a26-bc92-1002d48c1ee8","uuid":"b08bbf8f-f105-418a-9c9c-87285f97b257"}
[2026-03-16T01:35:29.072Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UVzksPLh8Q5sWkAVjZ1jti","type":"tool_result","content":"   500→\n   501→#### Test: Reserve button creates a booking when logged in\n   502→- **Initial state:** User is logged in, on a property detail page for another user's property. Check-in \"2026-05-01\", check-out \"2026-05-04\", and 2 guests are selected.\n   503→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Reserve\" button.\n   504→- **Expected:** The app calls `POST /api/bookings` with the property_id, check_in, check_out, num_guests, and total_price. A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Booking confirmed!\") and the user is redirected to the My Trips page (`/trips`), or a confirmation is shown on the same page.\n   505→\n   506→#### Test: Reserve button is disabled when dates are not selected\n   507→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on a property detail page. No dates have been selected.\n   508→- **Expected:** The \"Reserve\" button is disabled/grayed out and not clickable. A hint message like \"Select dates to book\" may be displayed.\n   509→\n   510→#### Test: Reserve button prompts login when user is not logged in\n   511→- **Initial state:** User is not logged in and is on a property detail page with valid dates and guests selected.\n   512→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Reserve\" button.\n   513→- **Expected:** The user is redirected to the login page (`/login`). Alternatively, a message like \"Please log in to book\" is displayed.\n   514→\n   515→#### Test: Reserve button is disabled for host's own property\n   516→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as the host of the current property. Dates and guests are selected.\n   517→- **Expected:** The \"Reserve\" button is disabled or hidden. A message like \"You cannot book your own property\" is displayed.\n   518→\n   519→#### Test: Check-in date picker prevents selecting past dates\n   520→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page.\n   521→- **Action:** User opens the check-in date picker.\n   522→- **Expected:** Dates before today are disabled/grayed out and cannot be selected.\n   523→\n   524→#### Test: Check-out date must be after check-in date\n   525→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page and has selected check-in \"2026-05-01\".\n   526→- **Action:** User opens the check-out date picker.\n   527→- **Expected:** Dates on or before \"2026-05-01\" are disabled/grayed out. Only dates after the check-in date are selectable.\n   528→\n   529→#### Test: Guest count cannot exceed property max_guests\n   530→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page for a property with max_guests 4.\n   531→- **Action:** User tries to set the guest count higher than 4.\n   532→- **Expected:** The guest count selector prevents selecting more than 4 guests. The maximum is capped at 4.\n   533→\n   534→#### Test: Guest count minimum is 1\n   535→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page.\n   536→- **Action:** User interacts with the guest count selector.\n   537→- **Expected:** The minimum selectable value is 1. The user cannot set guests to 0 or a negative number.\n   538→\n   539→#### Test: Reserve button shows error for unavailable dates\n   540→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on a property detail page. The property has an existing confirmed booking for \"2026-05-01\" to \"2026-05-04\".\n   541→- **Action:** User selects overlapping dates (e.g., check-in \"2026-05-02\", check-out \"2026-05-06\") and clicks \"Reserve\".\n   542→- **Expected:** An error message is displayed (e.g., \"Property is not available for the selected dates\"). The booking is not created.\n   543→\n   544→#### Test: Booking card is sticky on desktop viewport\n   545→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page on a desktop viewport.\n   546→- **Action:** User scrolls down the page past the booking card's initial position.\n   547→- **Expected:** The booking card remains visible in a sticky sidebar position as the user scrolls through the property description, amenities, and reviews.\n   548→\n   549→#### Test: Booking card date pickers and guest selector are functional on repeated use\n   550→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page.\n   551→- **Action:** User selects check-in \"2026-05-01\" and check-out \"2026-05-04\", then changes check-in to \"2026-06-01\" and check-out to \"2026-06-05\", then changes guest count from 2 to 4 and back to 2.\n   552→- **Expected:** Each change correctly updates the price breakdown. The final state shows \"2026-06-01\" to \"2026-06-05\" with 2 guests.\n   553→\n   554→### Component: ReviewsSection\n   555→\n   556→#### Test: Reviews section displays average ratings by category\n   557→- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id` for a property with multiple reviews. The average ratings are: cleanliness 4.5, accuracy 4.2, communication 4.8, location 4.6, value 4.0.\n   558→- **Expected:** The reviews section shows a summary with average ratings for each category: \"Cleanliness: 4.5\", \"Accuracy: 4.2\", \"Communication: 4.8\", \"Location: 4.6\", \"Value: 4.0\". Each rating is displayed with a star icon or progress bar. An overall average rating is also displayed.\n   559→\n   560→#### Test: Reviews section displays overall average rating and total review count\n   561→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page with 15 reviews and an overall average rating of 4.3.\n   562→- **Expected:** The reviews section header shows a star icon with \"4.3\" and \"15 reviews\" (or similar format like \"4.3 · 15 reviews\").\n   563→\n   564→#### Test: Reviews section displays individual review cards\n   565→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page with reviews. A review exists from guest \"Alice\" dated \"2026-01-15\" with rating 5 and comment \"Amazing place, loved every minute!\".\n   566→- **Expected:** An individual review card is displayed showing the guest name \"Alice\", the date \"January 2026\" (or similar formatted date), a star rating of 5, and the comment text \"Amazing place, loved every minute!\".\n   567→\n   568→#### Test: Review cards display guest avatar or initial\n   569→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page with reviews. A reviewer has an avatar_url set, another reviewer does not.\n   570→- **Expected:** Review cards show the guest's avatar image when available. When no avatar is set, a placeholder (e.g., first initial in a circle) is displayed.\n   571→\n   572→#### Test: Reviews section shows message when property has no reviews\n   573→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with no reviews.\n   574→- **Expected:** The reviews section displays a message like \"No reviews yet\" instead of an empty review list. Category average ratings are not shown.\n   575→\n   576→#### Test: Reviews section handles pagination or \"Show more\" for many reviews\n   577→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page with more than 6 reviews.\n   578→- **Expected:** An initial subset of reviews is displayed (e.g., 6 reviews). A \"Show all X reviews\" button is visible at the bottom (where X is the total count).\n   579→\n   580→#### Test: Clicking \"Show all reviews\" reveals all review cards\n   581→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page with more than 6 reviews and a \"Show all X reviews\" button visible.\n   582→- **Action:** User clicks \"Show all X reviews\".\n   583→- **Expected:** All review cards are displayed. The button disappears or changes to \"Show less\".\n   584→\n   585→#### Test: Reviews are ordered by most recent first\n   586→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page with multiple reviews created on different dates.\n   587→- **Expected:** Review cards are displayed in reverse chronological order, with the most recently created review appearing first.\n   588→\n   589→### Component: HostInfoCard\n   590→\n   591→#### Test: Host info card displays host name, avatar, bio, and member since date\n   592→- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id`. The property host has name \"Jane Host\", an avatar_url, bio \"Superhostess who loves sharing her properties\", and created_at \"2023-06-15\".\n   593→- **Expected:** The host info card displays: the host's avatar image, name \"Jane Host\", bio text \"Superhostess who loves sharing her properties\", and \"Member since June 2023\" (formatted from created_at).\n   594→\n   595→#### Test: Host info card displays number of listings\n   596→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page. The host has 5 active property listings.\n   597→- **Expected:** The host info card shows \"5 listings\" (or similar format like \"5 properties\").\n   598→\n   599→#### Test: Host info card shows placeholder avatar when host has no avatar\n   600→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page. The host has avatar_url set to null.\n   601→- **Expected:** A placeholder avatar (e.g., first initial in a circle or a generic person icon) is displayed instead of a broken image.\n   602→\n   603→#### Test: Host info card displays correctly when host has no bio\n   604→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page. The host has bio set to null.\n   605→- **Expected:** The host info card displays the host name, avatar, and member since date. The bio area is either not shown or displays a default message. No empty or broken layout.\n   606→\n   607→## Page: My Trips (`/trips`)\n   608→\n   609→<!-- Components: TripsTabs, TripCard, CancelBookingDialog -->\n   610→\n   611→### Component: TripsTabs\n   612→\n   613→#### Test: My Trips page requires login\n   614→- **Initial state:** User is not logged in.\n   615→- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips`.\n   616→- **Expected:** The user is redirected to the login page (`/login`). The My Trips page content is not displayed.\n   617→\n   618→#### Test: My Trips page defaults to Upcoming tab\n   619→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and navigates to `/trips`.\n   620→- **Expected:** The page displays three tabs: \"Upcoming\", \"Past\", and \"Cancelled\". The \"Upcoming\" tab is selected/highlighted by default. The content area shows upcoming trips (bookings with status \"pending\" or \"confirmed\" and check_in date >= today).\n   621→\n   622→#### Test: Upcoming tab shows pending and confirmed future bookings\n   623→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with bookings: a confirmed booking checking in next week, a pending booking checking in next month, a completed booking from last month, and a cancelled booking.\n   624→- **Action:** User is on the \"Upcoming\" tab.\n   625→- **Expected:** Only the confirmed and pending future bookings are displayed. Completed and cancelled bookings are not shown in this tab.\n   626→\n   627→#### Test: Switching to Past tab shows completed bookings\n   628→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page with the \"Upcoming\" tab selected. The user has completed bookings.\n   629→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Past\" tab.\n   630→- **Expected:** The \"Past\" tab becomes selected/highlighted. The content area updates to show only bookings with status \"completed\". Upcoming and cancelled bookings are not shown.\n   631→\n   632→#### Test: Switching to Cancelled tab shows cancelled bookings\n   633→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page with the \"Upcoming\" tab selected. The user has cancelled bookings.\n   634→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancelled\" tab.\n   635→- **Expected:** The \"Cancelled\" tab becomes selected/highlighted. The content area updates to show only bookings with status \"cancelled\". Upcoming and completed bookings are not shown.\n   636→\n   637→#### Test: Switching back to Upcoming tab from another tab\n   638→- **Initial state:** User is on the My Trips page with the \"Past\" tab selected.\n   639→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Upcoming\" tab.\n   640→- **Expected:** The \"Upcoming\" tab becomes selected/highlighted. The content area updates to show upcoming bookings again.\n   641→\n   642→#### Test: Tab shows empty state when no bookings exist for that category\n   643→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with no completed bookings.\n   644→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Past\" tab.\n   645→- **Expected:** The \"Past\" tab content area displays a message like \"No past trips\" or \"You don't have any past trips yet.\" instead of an empty list.\n   646→\n   647→#### Test: Upcoming tab empty state message\n   648→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with no pending or confirmed future bookings.\n   649→- **Action:** User views the \"Upcoming\" tab (default).\n   650→- **Expected:** The tab content area displays a message like \"No upcoming trips\" with a suggestion to browse properties (e.g., a link to the home page).\n   651→\n   652→#### Test: Cancelled tab empty state message\n   653→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with no cancelled bookings.\n   654→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancelled\" tab.\n   655→- **Expected:** The tab content area displays a message like \"No cancelled trips.\"\n   656→\n   657→#### Test: Tabs are functional on repeated use\n   658→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page.\n   659→- **Action:** User clicks \"Past\", then \"Cancelled\", then \"Upcoming\", then \"Past\" again.\n   660→- **Expected:** Each click correctly updates the selected tab highlight and displays the correct set of bookings. The final state shows the \"Past\" tab selected with completed bookings displayed.\n   661→\n   662→### Component: TripCard\n   663→\n   664→#### Test: Trip card displays all required information\n   665→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page. A booking exists for property \"Beach House\" in \"Malibu\" with check_in \"2026-05-01\", check_out \"2026-05-05\", status \"confirmed\", and total_price $800. The property has an image.\n   666→- **Expected:** The trip card displays: the property's main image, property title \"Beach House\", city \"Malibu\", dates \"May 1 – May 5, 2026\" (or similar formatted date range), a status badge showing \"Confirmed\" in green, and the total price \"$800\".\n   667→\n   668→#### Test: Trip card displays correct status badge colors\n   669→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page. Bookings exist with different statuses.\n   670→- **Expected:** Status badges use the correct colors: \"Pending\" badge in yellow, \"Confirmed\" badge in green, \"Cancelled\" badge in red, \"Completed\" badge in blue.\n   671→\n   672→#### Test: Trip card shows property image or placeholder\n   673→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page. One booking has a property with images, another has a property with no images.\n   674→- **Expected:** The trip card for the property with images shows the main property image. The trip card for the property without images shows a placeholder image.\n   675→\n   676→#### Test: Clicking trip card navigates to booking details\n   677→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page. A trip card is displayed for a booking with id \"booking-123\".\n   678→- **Action:** User clicks on the trip card (not the cancel or review button).\n   679→- **Expected:** The app navigates to a booking detail view showing full booking information including property details, dates, guest count, price breakdown, and special requests.\n   680→\n   681→#### Test: Cancel button appears on pending bookings\n   682→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. A booking with status \"pending\" is displayed.\n   683→- **Expected:** The trip card shows a \"Cancel\" button (or cancel icon button) that is clickable.\n   684→\n   685→#### Test: Cancel button appears on confirmed bookings\n   686→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. A booking with status \"confirmed\" is displayed.\n   687→- **Expected:** The trip card shows a \"Cancel\" button that is clickable.\n   688→\n   689→#### Test: Cancel button does not appear on completed bookings\n   690→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A booking with status \"completed\" is displayed.\n   691→- **Expected:** The trip card does not show a \"Cancel\" button.\n   692→\n   693→#### Test: Cancel button does not appear on already cancelled bookings\n   694→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Cancelled\" tab. A booking with status \"cancelled\" is displayed.\n   695→- **Expected:** The trip card does not show a \"Cancel\" button.\n   696→\n   697→#### Test: Write Review button appears on completed bookings without a review\n   698→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A booking with status \"completed\" exists that does not have an associated review.\n   699→- **Expected:** The trip card shows a \"Write Review\" button that is clickable.\n   700→\n   701→#### Test: Write Review button does not appear on completed bookings that already have a review\n   702→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A completed booking exists that already has an associated review.\n   703→- **Expected:** The trip card does not show a \"Write Review\" button. Instead, it may show \"Reviewed\" text or a checkmark indicating a review was already submitted.\n   704→\n   705→#### Test: Clicking Write Review button navigates to review page\n   706→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A completed booking with id \"booking-456\" has no review.\n   707→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Write Review\" button on that trip card.\n   708→- **Expected:** The app navigates to `/trips/booking-456/review` (the Write Review page).\n   709→\n   710→#### Test: Write Review button does not appear on pending, confirmed, or cancelled bookings\n   711→- **Initial state:** User is logged in. Bookings exist with statuses \"pending\", \"confirmed\", and \"cancelled\".\n   712→- **Expected:** None of these trip cards display a \"Write Review\" button. The button only appears for \"completed\" bookings.\n   713→\n   714→#### Test: Trip cards are ordered by check-in date\n   715→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. Multiple upcoming bookings exist with different check-in dates.\n   716→- **Expected:** Trip cards are displayed in chronological order by check-in date, with the soonest upcoming trip first.\n   717→\n   718→### Component: CancelBookingDialog\n   719→\n   720→#### Test: Clicking Cancel button opens confirmation dialog\n   721→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. A booking with status \"confirmed\" is displayed with a \"Cancel\" button.\n   722→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button on the trip card.\n   723→- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog/modal appears asking the user to confirm the cancellation. The dialog displays text like \"Are you sure you want to cancel this booking?\" with the property name and dates for context. Two buttons are visible: \"Confirm Cancel\" (or \"Yes, Cancel\") and \"Keep Booking\" (or \"No, Go Back\").\n   724→\n   725→#### Test: Confirming cancellation updates booking status to cancelled\n   726→- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a confirmed booking.\n   727→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Confirm Cancel\" (or \"Yes, Cancel\") button.\n   728→- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"cancelled\". The dialog closes. The trip card is removed from the \"Upcoming\" tab (or its status badge updates to \"Cancelled\" in red). A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Booking cancelled successfully\"). The booking now appears in the \"Cancelled\" tab.\n   729→\n   730→#### Test: Dismissing cancellation dialog keeps booking unchanged\n   731→- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a pending booking.\n   732→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Keep Booking\" (or \"No, Go Back\") button.\n   733→- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The booking remains in its original status (pending). No API call is made. The trip card is unchanged.\n   734→\n   735→#### Test: Closing the dialog via overlay click keeps booking unchanged\n   736→- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open.\n   737→- **Action:** User clicks outside the dialog (on the overlay/backdrop).\n   738→- **Expected:** The dialog closes without making any changes to the booking.\n   739→\n   740→#### Test: Cancel dialog shows property and date context\n   741→- **Initial state:** User clicks \"Cancel\" on a trip card for property \"Mountain Cabin\" with dates \"June 10 – June 15, 2026\".\n   742→- **Expected:** The confirmation dialog displays the property name \"Mountain Cabin\" and the booking dates \"June 10 – June 15, 2026\" so the user can confirm they are cancelling the correct booking.\n   743→\n   744→#### Test: After cancellation, booking moves from Upcoming to Cancelled tab\n   745→- **Initial state:** User is on the \"Upcoming\" tab with a confirmed booking for \"Beach House\".\n   746→- **Action:** User clicks \"Cancel\" on the \"Beach House\" trip card, then confirms the cancellation in the dialog.\n   747→- **Expected:** The \"Beach House\" trip card is removed from the \"Upcoming\" tab. User switches to the \"Cancelled\" tab and sees the \"Beach House\" booking with a red \"Cancelled\" status badge.\n   748→\n   749→#### Test: Cancel dialog is functional on repeated use\n   750→- **Initial state:** User is on the \"Upcoming\" tab with two cancellable bookings.\n   751→- **Action:** User clicks \"Cancel\" on the first booking, dismisses the dialog (clicks \"Keep Booking\"), then clicks \"Cancel\" on the second booking and confirms the cancellation.\n   752→- **Expected:** The first booking remains unchanged in the \"Upcoming\" tab. The second booking is cancelled and moves to the \"Cancelled\" tab. Each dialog open/close cycle works correctly.\n   753→\n   754→## Page: Host Dashboard (`/hosting`)\n   755→\n   756→<!-- Components: StatsOverview, ListingsTab, BookingsTab, AddListingForm -->\n   757→\n   758→### Component: StatsOverview\n   759→\n   760→#### Test: Host Dashboard requires login — redirects unauthenticated users\n   761→- **Initial state:** No user is logged in.\n   762→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   763→- **Expected:** The app redirects the user to `/login`. The Host Dashboard is not rendered.\n   764→\n   765→#### Test: Host Dashboard requires host status — shows upgrade prompt for non-hosts\n   766→- **Initial state:** A user is logged in with `is_host` set to false.\n   767→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   768→- **Expected:** The page displays a message indicating the user is not a host (e.g., \"You need to become a host to access this page\") with a link or button to navigate to their profile page (`/profile`) where they can become a host.\n   769→\n   770→#### Test: Stats overview displays total listings count\n   771→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with 5 active properties and 1 inactive property in the database.\n   772→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   773→- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays a \"Total Listings\" stat card showing \"5\" (only active listings counted). The card has a label \"Total Listings\" and a numeric value.\n   774→\n   775→#### Test: Stats overview displays active bookings count\n   776→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. Their properties have 3 bookings with status \"confirmed\", 2 with status \"pending\", and 4 with status \"completed\".\n   777→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   778→- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays an \"Active Bookings\" stat card showing \"5\" (pending + confirmed bookings). The card has a label \"Active Bookings\" and a numeric value.\n   779→\n   780→#### Test: Stats overview displays total earnings\n   781→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. Their properties have completed bookings with total_price values of $500, $750, and $1200.\n   782→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   783→- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays a \"Total Earnings\" stat card showing \"$2,450\" (sum of completed booking total prices). The value is formatted as currency.\n   784→\n   785→#### Test: Stats overview displays average rating\n   786→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. Their properties have reviews with overall ratings of 4, 5, 3, and 5.\n   787→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   788→- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays an \"Average Rating\" stat card showing \"4.3\" (average of all review ratings, rounded to one decimal). A star icon is displayed next to the value.\n   789→\n   790→#### Test: Stats overview shows zeros for a new host with no data\n   791→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with no properties, no bookings, and no reviews.\n   792→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   793→- **Expected:** All four stat cards display zero/empty values: \"Total Listings: 0\", \"Active Bookings: 0\", \"Total Earnings: $0\", and \"Average Rating: —\" (or \"N/A\" when no reviews exist).\n   794→\n   795→#### Test: Host Dashboard displays navigation tabs for Listings and Bookings\n   796→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host.\n   797→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   798→- **Expected:** Below the stats overview, two tabs are visible: \"Listings\" and \"Bookings\". The \"Listings\" tab is active/selected by default.\n   799→\n   800→#### Test: Switching between Listings and Bookings tabs\n   801→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host and on `/hosting` with the \"Listings\" tab active.\n   802→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Bookings\" tab.\n   803→- **Expected:** The Bookings tab content is displayed (table of bookings). The \"Bookings\" tab appears active/selected. User clicks \"Listings\" tab again and the listings grid is displayed.\n   804→\n   805→### Component: ListingsTab\n   806→\n   807→#### Test: Listings tab displays host's properties in a grid\n   808→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with 3 active properties: \"Beach House\" ($150/night), \"Mountain Cabin\" ($200/night), \"City Loft\" ($120/night).\n   809→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting` (Listings tab is active by default).\n   810→- **Expected:** A grid of 3 property cards is displayed. Each card shows the property title, main image, price per night, and status (active/inactive).\n   811→\n   812→#### Test: Listing card shows property details\n   813→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with a property: title \"Beach House\", price $150/night, city \"Malibu\", 4.5 average rating, 10 reviews, active status.\n   814→- **Expected:** The listing card displays the property title \"Beach House\", price \"$150/night\", location \"Malibu\", average rating \"4.5\" with star icon, review count \"10 reviews\", and a green \"Active\" badge.\n   815→\n   816→#### Test: Listing card has Edit button that navigates to property detail\n   817→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with a property (id \"prop-123\").\n   818→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Edit\" button on the property card.\n   819→- **Expected:** The app navigates to `/properties/prop-123` where the host can view and edit their property details.\n   820→\n   821→#### Test: Listing card has Deactivate button for active properties\n   822→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with an active property \"Beach House\".\n   823→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Deactivate\" button on the \"Beach House\" card.\n   824→- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears asking \"Are you sure you want to deactivate this listing?\". The dialog shows the property name \"Beach House\".\n   825→\n   826→#### Test: Confirming deactivation sets property to inactive\n   827→- **Initial state:** The deactivation confirmation dialog is open for \"Beach House\".\n   828→- **Action:** User clicks the confirm button (e.g., \"Yes, Deactivate\").\n   829→- **Expected:** The app calls `DELETE /api/properties/:id` (which sets `is_active` to false). The dialog closes. The property card updates to show an \"Inactive\" status badge (gray or muted). A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Listing deactivated\"). The stats overview updates the \"Total Listings\" count to reflect the change.\n   830→\n   831→#### Test: Dismissing deactivation dialog keeps property active\n   832→- **Initial state:** The deactivation confirmation dialog is open for \"Beach House\".\n   833→- **Action:** User clicks the dismiss/cancel button.\n   834→- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The property remains active with no changes.\n   835→\n   836→#### Test: Listing card shows Activate button for inactive properties\n   837→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with an inactive property \"Old Cabin\".\n   838→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Activate\" button on the \"Old Cabin\" card.\n   839→- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/properties/:id` to set `is_active` to true. The property card updates to show a green \"Active\" badge. The \"Total Listings\" stat updates.\n   840→\n   841→#### Test: Listings tab shows empty state for host with no properties\n   842→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with no properties.\n   843→- **Expected:** The Listings tab displays an empty state message (e.g., \"You don't have any listings yet\") and a prominent \"Add Listing\" button or call-to-action.\n   844→\n   845→#### Test: Add Listing button is visible on the Listings tab\n   846→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host.\n   847→- **Expected:** An \"Add Listing\" button is prominently displayed on the Listings tab (e.g., in the header area or as a floating action button). The button has clear text \"Add Listing\" or a \"+\" icon with label.\n   848→\n   849→#### Test: Deactivate and activate actions work on repeated use\n   850→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with two active properties.\n   851→- **Action:** User deactivates the first property (confirms dialog), then activates it again, then deactivates the second property.\n   852→- **Expected:** Each action updates the correct property's status. The stats overview correctly reflects the current count of active listings after each action.\n   853→\n   854→### Component: BookingsTab\n   855→\n   856→#### Test: Bookings tab displays table of bookings for host's properties\n   857→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. Their properties have bookings from various guests.\n   858→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Bookings\" tab.\n   859→- **Expected:** A table is displayed with columns: Property, Guest, Check-in, Check-out, Guests, Total, Status, and Actions. Each booking is a row in the table.\n   860→\n   861→#### Test: Bookings table shows correct data for each booking\n   862→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. A booking exists: property \"Beach House\", guest \"Alice Smith\", check-in \"2026-07-01\", check-out \"2026-07-05\", 2 guests, total $750, status \"confirmed\".\n   863→- **Expected:** The table row displays: \"Beach House\", \"Alice Smith\", \"Jul 1, 2026\", \"Jul 5, 2026\", \"2\", \"$750\", a green \"Confirmed\" status badge.\n   864→\n   865→#### Test: Bookings tab has status filter controls\n   866→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab.\n   867→- **Expected:** Filter controls are visible above the table allowing the host to filter by status: \"All\", \"Pending\", \"Confirmed\", \"Cancelled\", \"Completed\". \"All\" is selected by default.\n   868→\n   869→#### Test: Filtering bookings by Pending status\n   870→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. Bookings exist with statuses \"pending\", \"confirmed\", and \"completed\".\n   871→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Pending\" status filter.\n   872→- **Expected:** Only bookings with status \"pending\" are displayed in the table. The \"Pending\" filter appears active/selected.\n   873→\n   874→#### Test: Filtering bookings by Confirmed status\n   875→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab with various bookings.\n   876→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Confirmed\" status filter.\n   877→- **Expected:** Only bookings with status \"confirmed\" are shown. Other bookings are hidden.\n   878→\n   879→#### Test: Filtering bookings by Completed status\n   880→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab with various bookings.\n   881→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Completed\" status filter.\n   882→- **Expected:** Only bookings with status \"completed\" are shown.\n   883→\n   884→#### Test: Filtering bookings by Cancelled status\n   885→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab with various bookings.\n   886→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancelled\" status filter.\n   887→- **Expected:** Only bookings with status \"cancelled\" are shown.\n   888→\n   889→#### Test: Resetting filter to All shows all bookings\n   890→- **Initial state:** User is on the Bookings tab with the \"Pending\" filter active.\n   891→- **Action:** User clicks the \"All\" filter.\n   892→- **Expected:** All bookings across all statuses are displayed again.\n   893→\n   894→#### Test: Status filters work on repeated use\n   895→- **Initial state:** User is on the Bookings tab with various bookings.\n   896→- **Action:** User clicks \"Pending\", then \"Confirmed\", then \"All\", then \"Completed\".\n   897→- **Expected:** Each filter correctly shows the appropriate subset of bookings. The active filter indicator updates correctly each time.\n   898→\n   899→#### Test: Host can confirm a pending booking"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015mHckA24UDTvDqWytokBhE","session_id":"d8954074-381a-4a26-bc92-1002d48c1ee8","uuid":"bf3fff82-83c2-4156-ac64-0fdd9669cd01"}
