[2026-03-16T01:35:30.571Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P4wFgEMHG7LEop4TDerxzA","type":"tool_result","content":"   900→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. A booking with status \"pending\" for guest \"Bob\" at property \"Beach House\" is displayed.\n   901→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Confirm\" button on that booking row.\n   902→- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"confirmed\". The booking's status badge changes from yellow \"Pending\" to green \"Confirmed\". The \"Confirm\" button is no longer visible for that booking. A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Booking confirmed\"). The \"Active Bookings\" stat in StatsOverview remains accurate.\n   903→\n   904→#### Test: Host can cancel a pending booking\n   905→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. A pending booking is displayed.\n   906→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button on the pending booking row.\n   907→- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears asking the host to confirm cancellation. The dialog shows the guest name, property, and dates for context.\n   908→\n   909→#### Test: Confirming cancellation of a booking updates status\n   910→- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a pending booking.\n   911→- **Action:** User clicks the confirm button in the dialog.\n   912→- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"cancelled\". The dialog closes. The booking's status badge changes to red \"Cancelled\". The \"Cancel\" and \"Confirm\" action buttons are removed for that booking. A success message is displayed. The \"Active Bookings\" stat decreases by 1.\n   913→\n   914→#### Test: Dismissing booking cancellation dialog keeps booking unchanged\n   915→- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a booking.\n   916→- **Action:** User clicks the dismiss button or clicks outside the dialog.\n   917→- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The booking status remains unchanged.\n   918→\n   919→#### Test: Host can cancel a confirmed booking\n   920→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. A booking with status \"confirmed\" is displayed.\n   921→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button on the confirmed booking row and confirms in the dialog.\n   922→- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"cancelled\". The status badge changes to red \"Cancelled\". The \"Active Bookings\" stat decreases.\n   923→\n   924→#### Test: Completed and cancelled bookings have no action buttons\n   925→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. Bookings exist with statuses \"completed\" and \"cancelled\".\n   926→- **Expected:** Booking rows with \"completed\" or \"cancelled\" status do not display \"Confirm\" or \"Cancel\" action buttons. Only pending and confirmed bookings show action buttons.\n   927→\n   928→#### Test: Bookings tab shows empty state when no bookings exist\n   929→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with properties but no bookings.\n   930→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Bookings\" tab.\n   931→- **Expected:** The tab displays an empty state message (e.g., \"No bookings yet\").\n   932→\n   933→#### Test: Status badges display correct colors\n   934→- **Initial state:** User is on the Bookings tab with bookings in all four statuses.\n   935→- **Expected:** Status badges use the correct colors: \"Pending\" has a yellow badge, \"Confirmed\" has a green badge, \"Cancelled\" has a red badge, \"Completed\" has a blue badge.\n   936→\n   937→#### Test: Confirm and cancel actions work on repeated use\n   938→- **Initial state:** User is on the Bookings tab with three pending bookings.\n   939→- **Action:** User confirms the first booking, cancels the second booking (confirming the dialog), and then confirms the third booking.\n   940→- **Expected:** Each action updates the correct booking. The first and third show \"Confirmed\" badges, the second shows \"Cancelled\". Stats update correctly after each action.\n   941→\n   942→### Component: AddListingForm\n   943→\n   944→#### Test: Clicking Add Listing button opens the multi-step form\n   945→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Listings tab.\n   946→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Add Listing\" button.\n   947→- **Expected:** A multi-step form opens (modal or full-page). Step 1 is displayed with fields for property type and title. A step indicator shows progress (Step 1 of 7). \"Next\" and \"Cancel\" buttons are visible.\n   948→\n   949→#### Test: Step 1 — Property type selection and title input\n   950→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is open on Step 1.\n   951→- **Expected:** A dropdown or selection control lists property types: \"Apartment\", \"House\", \"Cabin\", \"Villa\", \"Condo\", \"Loft\", \"Cottage\", \"Townhouse\". A text input field for the property title is visible. Both fields are required.\n   952→\n   953→#### Test: Step 1 — Selecting property type and entering title\n   954→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 1.\n   955→- **Action:** User selects \"Cabin\" from the property type selector and types \"Cozy Mountain Retreat\" in the title field.\n   956→- **Expected:** The property type shows \"Cabin\" selected. The title field displays \"Cozy Mountain Retreat\". The \"Next\" button becomes enabled (or was already enabled).\n   957→\n   958→#### Test: Step 1 — Validation prevents proceeding without required fields\n   959→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 1 with no selections made.\n   960→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\" without selecting a property type or entering a title.\n   961→- **Expected:** Validation errors are displayed for both fields (e.g., \"Property type is required\", \"Title is required\"). The form does not advance to Step 2.\n   962→\n   963→#### Test: Step 2 — Location fields displayed\n   964→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 1 and clicked \"Next\".\n   965→- **Expected:** Step 2 is displayed with fields for: address (with geocoding/autocomplete), city, state, and country. A \"Back\" button and \"Next\" button are visible. The step indicator shows Step 2 of 7.\n   966→\n   967→#### Test: Step 2 — Address field uses autocomplete\n   968→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 2.\n   969→- **Action:** User types \"123 Main\" in the address field.\n   970→- **Expected:** An autocomplete dropdown appears with address suggestions from a geocoding API (e.g., OpenStreetMap Nominatim). Selecting a suggestion populates the address field with the full address.\n   971→\n   972→#### Test: Step 2 — Address autocomplete populates related fields\n   973→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 2.\n   974→- **Action:** User types in the address field and selects an autocomplete suggestion for \"123 Main St, Denver, CO, USA\".\n   975→- **Expected:** The address field is populated with \"123 Main St\". The city field is auto-filled with \"Denver\". The state field is auto-filled with \"CO\". The country field is auto-filled with \"USA\".\n   976→\n   977→#### Test: Step 2 — Validation requires city and country\n   978→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 2 with address filled but city and country empty.\n   979→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\".\n   980→- **Expected:** Validation errors appear for city and country (e.g., \"City is required\", \"Country is required\"). The form does not advance.\n   981→\n   982→#### Test: Step 3 — Details fields displayed\n   983→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 2 and clicked \"Next\".\n   984→- **Expected:** Step 3 is displayed with numeric input fields for: max guests, bedrooms, beds, and bathrooms. Each field has increment/decrement controls or is a number input. The step indicator shows Step 3 of 7.\n   985→\n   986→#### Test: Step 3 — Setting property details\n   987→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 3.\n   988→- **Action:** User sets max guests to 4, bedrooms to 2, beds to 3, bathrooms to 1.\n   989→- **Expected:** All fields display the entered values. The \"Next\" button is enabled.\n   990→\n   991→#### Test: Step 3 — Validation requires all detail fields\n   992→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 3 with all fields at 0 or empty.\n   993→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\".\n   994→- **Expected:** Validation errors appear (e.g., \"Max guests must be at least 1\"). The form does not advance.\n   995→\n   996→#### Test: Step 4 — Amenities selection displayed\n   997→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 3 and clicked \"Next\".\n   998→- **Expected:** Step 4 is displayed with checkboxes for amenities grouped by category: \"Essentials\", \"Features\", \"Safety\", \"Location\". Each category heading is visible with its amenities listed below. The step indicator shows Step 4 of 7.\n   999→\n  1000→#### Test: Step 4 — Selecting amenities\n  1001→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 4 with amenities loaded from `GET /api/amenities`.\n  1002→- **Action:** User checks \"WiFi\" and \"Kitchen\" under Essentials, and \"Pool\" under Features.\n  1003→- **Expected:** The selected amenities show as checked. The user can proceed to the next step. Amenities are optional (no validation error if none selected).\n  1004→\n  1005→#### Test: Step 4 — Amenities are toggleable\n  1006→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 4 with \"WiFi\" already checked.\n  1007→- **Action:** User clicks \"WiFi\" to uncheck it, then checks it again.\n  1008→- **Expected:** The checkbox toggles correctly on each click.\n  1009→\n  1010→#### Test: Step 5 — Photo URL input displayed\n  1011→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 4 and clicked \"Next\".\n  1012→- **Expected:** Step 5 is displayed with an input field for image URLs and an \"Add Photo\" button. A list/grid of added photos is shown below (initially empty). The step indicator shows Step 5 of 7.\n  1013→\n  1014→#### Test: Step 5 — Adding a photo URL\n  1015→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 5.\n  1016→- **Action:** User types \"https://example.com/photo1.jpg\" in the URL input and clicks \"Add Photo\".\n  1017→- **Expected:** The photo URL is added to the list. A preview or thumbnail of the image is displayed. The URL input is cleared for the next entry. An optional caption field may be shown for the added photo.\n  1018→\n  1019→#### Test: Step 5 — Adding multiple photo URLs\n  1020→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 5 with one photo already added.\n  1021→- **Action:** User adds two more photo URLs.\n  1022→- **Expected:** All three photos are displayed in the list/grid. Each photo can be reordered or removed.\n  1023→\n  1024→#### Test: Step 5 — Removing a photo\n  1025→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 5 with 3 photos added.\n  1026→- **Action:** User clicks the remove/delete button on the second photo.\n  1027→- **Expected:** The second photo is removed from the list. The remaining 2 photos are displayed.\n  1028→\n  1029→#### Test: Step 5 — Validation requires at least one photo\n  1030→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 5 with no photos added.\n  1031→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\".\n  1032→- **Expected:** A validation error appears (e.g., \"At least one photo is required\"). The form does not advance.\n  1033→\n  1034→#### Test: Step 6 — Pricing fields displayed\n  1035→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 5 and clicked \"Next\".\n  1036→- **Expected:** Step 6 is displayed with numeric input fields for: price per night and cleaning fee. The price per night field is required. The cleaning fee defaults to 0. Currency formatting or prefix ($) is shown. The step indicator shows Step 6 of 7.\n  1037→\n  1038→#### Test: Step 6 — Entering pricing information\n  1039→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 6.\n  1040→- **Action:** User enters 150 for price per night and 50 for cleaning fee.\n  1041→- **Expected:** The fields display $150 and $50 respectively.\n  1042→\n  1043→#### Test: Step 6 — Validation requires price per night\n  1044→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 6 with price per night empty or 0.\n  1045→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\".\n  1046→- **Expected:** A validation error appears (e.g., \"Price per night is required and must be greater than 0\"). The form does not advance.\n  1047→\n  1048→#### Test: Step 7 — Review and publish page displayed\n  1049→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 6 and clicked \"Next\".\n  1050→- **Expected:** Step 7 displays a summary of all entered information: property type, title, full address (address, city, state, country), details (guests, bedrooms, beds, bathrooms), selected amenities, photo thumbnails, price per night, and cleaning fee. A \"Publish\" button and \"Back\" button are visible. The step indicator shows Step 7 of 7.\n  1051→\n  1052→#### Test: Step 7 — Review page shows all entered data correctly\n  1053→- **Initial state:** User has filled out all steps: type \"Cabin\", title \"Cozy Mountain Retreat\", address \"123 Pine Rd, Aspen, CO, USA\", 4 guests, 2 bedrooms, 2 beds, 1 bathroom, amenities \"WiFi\" and \"Kitchen\", 2 photos, price $200/night, cleaning fee $75.\n  1054→- **Expected:** The review page displays all of these values accurately. No data is missing or incorrect.\n  1055→\n  1056→#### Test: Publishing a new listing creates the property\n  1057→- **Initial state:** User is on Step 7 (Review) with all data entered correctly.\n  1058→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Publish\" button.\n  1059→- **Expected:** The app calls `POST /api/properties` with the property data, then `POST /api/property-images` for each photo. A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Listing published successfully!\"). The form closes. The new property appears in the Listings tab grid. The \"Total Listings\" stat increments by 1.\n  1060→\n  1061→#### Test: Back button navigates to the previous step\n  1062→- **Initial state:** User is on Step 3 of the Add Listing form.\n  1063→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Back\" button.\n  1064→- **Expected:** The form navigates to Step 2. All previously entered data in Step 2 is preserved (city, address, etc. are still filled).\n  1065→\n  1066→#### Test: Cancel button closes the form without saving\n  1067→- **Initial state:** User is on Step 4 of the Add Listing form with data entered in Steps 1–3.\n  1068→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button.\n  1069→- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears asking \"Discard your listing? All entered information will be lost.\" with \"Discard\" and \"Keep Editing\" buttons.\n  1070→\n  1071→#### Test: Confirming cancel discards the listing form\n  1072→- **Initial state:** The discard confirmation dialog is open.\n  1073→- **Action:** User clicks \"Discard\".\n  1074→- **Expected:** The form closes. No API calls are made. The user returns to the Listings tab. No new property is created.\n  1075→\n  1076→#### Test: Dismissing cancel keeps the form open\n  1077→- **Initial state:** The discard confirmation dialog is open.\n  1078→- **Action:** User clicks \"Keep Editing\".\n  1079→- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The form remains on the current step with all data preserved.\n  1080→\n  1081→#### Test: Step indicator shows correct progress throughout the form\n  1082→- **Initial state:** User opens the Add Listing form.\n  1083→- **Action:** User navigates through all 7 steps using Next/Back buttons.\n  1084→- **Expected:** The step indicator accurately shows the current step (e.g., \"Step 1 of 7\", \"Step 2 of 7\", etc.) at each stage. Completed steps may show a checkmark or different styling.\n  1085→\n  1086→#### Test: Data persistence across steps when navigating back and forth\n  1087→- **Initial state:** User has filled out Steps 1–5 and is on Step 5.\n  1088→- **Action:** User clicks \"Back\" twice to Step 3, then \"Next\" twice to Step 5.\n  1089→- **Expected:** All data entered in Steps 3, 4, and 5 is preserved after navigating back and forth. No data is lost.\n  1090→\n  1091→#### Test: Add Listing form works correctly on repeated use\n  1092→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. User has already published one listing successfully.\n  1093→- **Action:** User clicks \"Add Listing\" again, fills out all steps, and publishes.\n  1094→- **Expected:** A second property is created successfully. Both properties appear in the Listings tab. The \"Total Listings\" stat shows the correct total.\n  1095→\n  1096→## Page: User Profile (`/profile`)\n  1097→\n  1098→<!-- Components: ProfileForm, BecomeHostButton, UserReviewsList -->\n  1099→\n  1100→### Component: ProfileForm\n  1101→\n  1102→#### Test: Profile page requires login\n  1103→- **Initial state:** User is not logged in.\n  1104→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1105→- **Expected:** The user is redirected to `/login`. The profile page is not displayed.\n  1106→\n  1107→#### Test: Profile page displays current user info\n  1108→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with name \"Alice Smith\", email \"alice@example.com\", bio \"Love traveling!\", phone \"555-1234\", avatar URL \"https://example.com/avatar.jpg\".\n  1109→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1110→- **Expected:** The profile form displays the current values: name \"Alice Smith\", email \"alice@example.com\" (read-only), bio \"Love traveling!\", phone \"555-1234\", and avatar URL \"https://example.com/avatar.jpg\". The avatar image is displayed using the URL.\n  1111→\n  1112→#### Test: Edit name field inline\n  1113→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with name \"Alice Smith\".\n  1114→- **Action:** User clicks the name field, clears it, types \"Alice Johnson\", and clicks the \"Save\" button.\n  1115→- **Expected:** A `PUT /api/users/:id` request is sent with the updated name. The name field displays \"Alice Johnson\". A success message (e.g., \"Profile updated\") is shown. The Redux user state is updated with the new name.\n  1116→\n  1117→#### Test: Edit bio field inline\n  1118→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with bio \"Love traveling!\".\n  1119→- **Action:** User clicks the bio textarea, clears it, types \"Digital nomad and foodie\", and clicks \"Save\".\n  1120→- **Expected:** A `PUT /api/users/:id` request is sent with the updated bio. The bio field displays \"Digital nomad and foodie\". A success message is shown.\n  1121→\n  1122→#### Test: Edit phone field inline\n  1123→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with phone \"555-1234\".\n  1124→- **Action:** User clicks the phone field, clears it, types \"555-9876\", and clicks \"Save\".\n  1125→- **Expected:** A `PUT /api/users/:id` request is sent with the updated phone. The phone field displays \"555-9876\". A success message is shown.\n  1126→\n  1127→#### Test: Edit avatar URL field inline\n  1128→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with avatar URL \"https://example.com/old-avatar.jpg\".\n  1129→- **Action:** User clicks the avatar URL field, clears it, types \"https://example.com/new-avatar.jpg\", and clicks \"Save\".\n  1130→- **Expected:** A `PUT /api/users/:id` request is sent with the updated avatar URL. The avatar image preview updates to show the new image from \"https://example.com/new-avatar.jpg\". A success message is shown.\n  1131→\n  1132→#### Test: Save with empty name shows validation error\n  1133→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile`.\n  1134→- **Action:** User clears the name field (leaving it empty) and clicks \"Save\".\n  1135→- **Expected:** A validation error message is displayed (e.g., \"Name is required\"). No API call is made. The name field is highlighted as invalid.\n  1136→\n  1137→#### Test: Save with invalid avatar URL shows validation error\n  1138→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile`.\n  1139→- **Action:** User enters \"not-a-url\" in the avatar URL field and clicks \"Save\".\n  1140→- **Expected:** A validation error message is displayed (e.g., \"Please enter a valid URL\"). No API call is made.\n  1141→\n  1142→#### Test: Profile form fields are functional on repeated edits\n  1143→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with name \"Alice Smith\".\n  1144→- **Action:** User changes the name to \"Alice Johnson\" and clicks \"Save\". After the success message, user changes the name again to \"Alice Williams\" and clicks \"Save\".\n  1145→- **Expected:** Both saves succeed with separate `PUT /api/users/:id` requests. After the second save, the name field displays \"Alice Williams\". Both updates are persisted.\n  1146→\n  1147→#### Test: Email field is displayed but not editable\n  1148→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with email \"alice@example.com\".\n  1149→- **Action:** User views the profile form.\n  1150→- **Expected:** The email \"alice@example.com\" is displayed but the field is read-only / disabled and cannot be edited.\n  1151→\n  1152→#### Test: Profile update persists across navigation\n  1153→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with bio \"Old bio\".\n  1154→- **Action:** User changes bio to \"New bio\", clicks \"Save\", then navigates to `/` (home page), then navigates back to `/profile`.\n  1155→- **Expected:** The bio field displays \"New bio\", confirming the change was persisted to the database and Redux state.\n  1156→\n  1157→### Component: BecomeHostButton\n  1158→\n  1159→#### Test: Become a Host button is visible for non-host users\n  1160→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false`.\n  1161→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1162→- **Expected:** A \"Become a Host\" button is visible on the profile page.\n  1163→\n  1164→#### Test: Become a Host button is hidden for existing hosts\n  1165→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `true`.\n  1166→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1167→- **Expected:** The \"Become a Host\" button is NOT visible on the profile page.\n  1168→\n  1169→#### Test: Clicking Become a Host sets user as host\n  1170→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false` and on `/profile`.\n  1171→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Become a Host\" button.\n  1172→- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears (e.g., \"Are you sure you want to become a host?\"). User confirms. A `POST /api/users/:id/become-host` request is sent. Upon success, the button disappears, a success message is shown (e.g., \"You are now a host!\"), and the Redux user state updates `is_host` to `true`. The \"Hosting\" link becomes available in the navigation sidebar.\n  1173→\n  1174→#### Test: Cancel Become a Host confirmation dialog\n  1175→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false` and on `/profile`. The \"Become a Host\" button is visible.\n  1176→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Become a Host\" button, then clicks \"Cancel\" in the confirmation dialog.\n  1177→- **Expected:** The dialog closes. No API call is made. The \"Become a Host\" button remains visible. `is_host` remains `false`.\n  1178→\n  1179→#### Test: Become a Host button appearance\n  1180→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false` and on `/profile`.\n  1181→- **Action:** User views the profile page.\n  1182→- **Expected:** The \"Become a Host\" button is styled with the coral/red accent color (#FF5A5F), has clear text reading \"Become a Host\", and is visually prominent on the page.\n  1183→\n  1184→### Component: UserReviewsList\n  1185→\n  1186→#### Test: Reviews list displays user's written reviews\n  1187→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written 3 reviews for different properties (e.g., \"Cozy Cabin\" rated 5, \"City Apartment\" rated 3, \"Beach Villa\" rated 4).\n  1188→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1189→- **Expected:** A \"My Reviews\" section is visible showing all 3 reviews. Each review card displays: the property title, the overall rating (with filled/unfilled stars), the comment text, and the date the review was written.\n  1190→\n  1191→#### Test: Reviews list shows empty state for user with no reviews\n  1192→- **Initial state:** User is logged in but has not written any reviews.\n  1193→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1194→- **Expected:** The \"My Reviews\" section displays an empty state message (e.g., \"You haven't written any reviews yet\") instead of review cards.\n  1195→\n  1196→#### Test: Review card shows rating with star display\n  1197→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written a review with overall rating 4 out of 5.\n  1198→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1199→- **Expected:** The review card displays 4 filled stars and 1 unfilled star, matching the rating value."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015mHckA24UDTvDqWytokBhE","session_id":"d8954074-381a-4a26-bc92-1002d48c1ee8","uuid":"a4a3cb93-4ca6-4a19-a277-a2e98b3d2015"}
