d on the My Trips page.\n662:### Component: TripCard\n665:- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page. A booking exists for property \"Beach House\" in \"Malibu\" with check_in \"2026-05-01\", check_out \"2026-05-05\", status \"confirmed\", and total_price $800. The property has an image.\n669:- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page. Bookings exist with different statuses.\n673:- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page. One booking has a property with images, another has a property with no images.\n677:- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page. A trip card is displayed for a booking with id \"booking-123\".\n718:### Component: CancelBookingDialog\n1265:- **Expected:** The page displays a message such as \"You have already reviewed this booking\" and does not show the review form. Optionally shows a link back to My Trips.\n1336:- **Expected:** The review is submitted successfully via `POST /api/reviews`. The app navigates back to `/trips` (My Trips page). A success notification or message such as \"Review submitted successfully\" appears.\n1362:#### Test: Write Review button on My Trips disappears after submitting review\n1363:- **Initial state:** User has a completed booking for \"Oceanfront Villa\" showing a \"Write Review\" button on the My Trips page.\n1380:- **Expected:** The page displays a message such as \"You have already reviewed this booking\" instead of the review form. A link to return to My Trips is available.","numLines":22}}
